tight\">32</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>Overflow <em>is</em> the wrap of the phase, so unsigned integer arithmetic does it for free. The frequency resolution is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">32</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> = 100 kHz, 23 µHz. To get <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span>, use <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">round</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">32</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-lookup-table\">The lookup table</h2>\n<p>Only the top bits of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span> index the sine table: with 256 entries, <code>lut[A &gt;&gt; 24]</code>. The table is 12-bit values for the DAC, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">lut</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">round</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2047.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2047.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span><span class=\"mord\">/256</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span></span></span></span>. Throwing away the low 24 bits (<strong>phase truncation</strong>) adds a small periodic error, which shows up as spurs in the spectrum; interpolating between neighbouring entries, or a bigger table, reduces it. Nyquist still applies: keep <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">out</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> well below <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span></span>, in practice under about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, and follow the DAC with a reconstruction low-pass filter.</p>\n<p>On an STM32 the sample clock is a timer that triggers the DAC, and DMA feeds it from a buffer that the DDS loop refills, like the ADC in reverse (lesson 13).</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"dds\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>The phase accumulator as a sawtooth (top) and the DAC output from the table (bottom), sample by sample. Change the tuning word: the frequency is exactly M·f_s/2³².</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> = 100 kHz, target 1 kHz.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">round</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">32</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">5</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">42</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">949</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">673</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">out</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">42</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">949</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">673</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">5</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">32</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1000.0000003</span></span></span></span> Hz.</li>\n<li>Resolution <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">5</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">32</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">23.3</span></span></span></span> µHz.</li>\n<li>For 12.345 kHz, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> = 530 213 713 and the error is far below 0.1 %.</li>\n<li>Each output cycle has <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">100</span></span></span></span> samples; at 40 kHz, only 2.5, so the stair-step needs a good filter.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">dds.c</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdlib.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;math.h&gt;</span></span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> PI 3.14159265358979323846</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint16_t</span> lut[<span class=\"hljs-number\">256</span>];\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">lut_init</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span>)</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; i &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">256</span>; i++) lut[i] = (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint16_t</span>)lround(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2047.5</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">2047.5</span> * <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sin</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * PI * i / <span class=\"hljs-number\">256</span>)); }\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"hljs-class\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> {</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> acc, tuning; } <span class=\"hljs-type\">dds_t</span>;\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">dds_tuning</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> f, <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> fs)</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span>)llround(f * <span class=\"hljs-number\">4294967296.0</span> / fs); }\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint16_t</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">dds_next</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">dds_t</span> *d)</span> { <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint16_t</span> v = lut[d-&gt;acc &gt;&gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span>]; d-&gt;acc += d-&gt;tuning; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> v; }   <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* wraps mod 2^32 */</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* frequency from rising zero crossings of the DAC samples, with linear interpolation */</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">measure</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint16_t</span> *x, <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> n, <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> fs)</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> first = <span class=\"hljs-number\">-1</span>, last = <span class=\"hljs-number\">-1</span>; <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> crossings = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; <span class=\"hljs-type\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> mid = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2047.5</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>; i &lt; n; i++)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (x[i - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] &lt; mid &amp;&amp; x[i] &gt;= mid) {\n      <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> t = (i - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) + (mid - x[i - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]) / (<span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span>)(x[i] - x[i - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]);\n      <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (first &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>) first = t;\n      last = t; crossings++;\n    }\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> (crossings - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) / ((last - first) / fs);\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> CHECK(c) do { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (!(c)) { printf(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;FAIL line %d: %s\\n&quot;</span>, __LINE__, #c); exit(1); } } while (0)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">main</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span>)</span> {\n  lut_init();\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> fs = <span class=\"hljs-number\">100e3</span>; <span class=\"hljs-type\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> n = <span class=\"hljs-number\">100000</span>;            <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* 1 s of samples */</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint16_t</span> out[<span class=\"hljs-number\">100000</span>];\n  CHECK(dds_tuning(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>, fs) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">42949673u</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> targets[] = {<span class=\"hljs-number\">5.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2500.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">12345.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">30000.0</span>};\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> k = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; k &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">6</span>; k++) {\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">dds_t</span> d = {<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, dds_tuning(targets[k], fs)};\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; i &lt; n; i++) out[i] = dds_next(&amp;d);\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> exact = d.tuning * fs / <span class=\"hljs-number\">4294967296.0</span>, meas = measure(out, n, fs);\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> err = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">fabs</span>(meas - targets[k]) / targets[k];\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;target %9.3f Hz  M=%10u  exact %.6f Hz  measured %.4f Hz  (%.5f %%)\\n&quot;</span>, targets[k], d.tuning, exact, meas, <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span> * err);\n    CHECK(err &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.001</span>);                                      <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* within 0.1 % */</span>\n    CHECK(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">fabs</span>(exact - targets[k]) &lt;= fs / <span class=\"hljs-number\">4294967296.0</span>);    <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* within one resolution step */</span>\n  }\n  <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* amplitude and shape: the output tracks an ideal sine to within the table&#x27;s phase step */</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">dds_t</span> d = {<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, dds_tuning(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>, fs)}; <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> worst = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; i &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>; i++) {\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> a = d.acc; <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> ideal = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2047.5</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">2047.5</span> * <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sin</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * PI * (a / <span class=\"hljs-number\">4294967296.0</span>));\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> e = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">fabs</span>(dds_next(&amp;d) - ideal); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (e &gt; worst) worst = e;\n  }\n  <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;worst deviation from the ideal sine: %.1f LSB (bound 2047.5*2*pi/256 = %.1f)\\n&quot;</span>, worst, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2047.5</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * PI / <span class=\"hljs-number\">256</span>);\n  CHECK(worst &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">2047.5</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * PI / <span class=\"hljs-number\">256</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>);\n  CHECK(lut[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] == <span class=\"hljs-number\">2048</span> &amp;&amp; lut[<span class=\"hljs-number\">64</span>] == <span class=\"hljs-number\">4095</span> &amp;&amp; lut[<span class=\"hljs-number\">192</span>] == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS\\n&quot;</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>You need to sweep from 100 Hz to 10 kHz smoothly over 1 second. How does DDS make that easy, and why is there no click when the frequency changes?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Change the tuning word each sample (a linear ramp of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> gives a linear chirp). The accumulator’s phase is continuous, because only its <em>rate</em> changes, so the waveform never jumps. Switching between two fixed tables would create a phase discontinuity, which you’d hear as a click.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does the worst-case error check use <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2047.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord\">/256</span></span></span></span>?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Truncating the phase to 8 bits can be off by up to one table step, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord\">/256</span></span></span></span> rad. The sine’s steepest slope is its amplitude, 2047.5 LSB per radian, so the worst error is about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2047.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord\">/256</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50</span></span></span></span> LSB, plus half an LSB of rounding. Linear interpolation between entries would cut it to below 1 LSB.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p10-l14\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"the-phase-accumulator","title":"The phase accumulator"},{"id":"the-lookup-table","title":"The lookup table"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p10-l14-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Tuning word for 1 kHz at f_s = 100 kHz with a 32-bit accumulator?</p>\n","explain":"<p>f·2³²/f_s.</p>\n","answer":42949673,"tol":1e-7,"unit":""},{"id":"p10-l14-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Frequency resolution in µHz at f_s = 100 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>f_s/2³².</p>\n","answer":23.28,"tol":0.001,"unit":"µHz"},{"id":"p10-l14-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Output frequency in Hz for M = 2^24 at f_s = 100 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>One table entry per sample.</p>\n","answer":390.625,"tol":0.001,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p10-l14-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Samples per cycle at 12.345 kHz with f_s = 100 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>f_s/f.</p>\n","answer":8.1,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p10-l14-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>What happens when the accumulator overflows?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Unsigned overflow is modulo 2³².</p>\n","options":["the frequency doubles","the output glitches","nothing special, it is the phase wrapping through 2π","the DAC resets"],"answer":2},{"id":"p10-l14-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Which bits of the accumulator index a 256-entry table?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The most significant bits are the coarse phase.</p>\n","options":["the low 8 bits","the top 8 bits","all 32","bits 8 to 15"],"answer":1}],"code":[{"file":"dds.c","lang":"c","src":"#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define PI 3.14159265358979323846\nstatic uint16_t lut[256];\nstatic void lut_init(void) { for (int i = 0; i < 256; i++) lut[i] = (uint16_t)lround(2047.5 + 2047.5 * sin(2 * PI * i / 256)); }\n\ntypedef struct { uint32_t acc, tuning; } dds_t;\nstatic uint32_t dds_tuning(double f, double fs) { return (uint32_t)llround(f * 4294967296.0 / fs); }\nstatic uint16_t dds_next(dds_t *d) { uint16_t v = lut[d->acc >> 24]; d->acc += d->tuning; return v; }   /* wraps mod 2^32 */\n\n/* frequency from rising zero crossings of the DAC samples, with linear interpolation */\nstatic double measure(const uint16_t *x, int n, double fs) {\n  double first = -1, last = -1; int crossings = 0; const double mid = 2047.5;\n  for (int i = 1; i < n; i++)\n    if (x[i - 1] < mid && x[i] >= mid) {\n      double t = (i - 1) + (mid - x[i - 1]) / (double)(x[i] - x[i - 1]);\n      if (first < 0) first = t;\n      last = t; crossings++;\n    }\n  return (crossings - 1) / ((last - first) / fs);\n}\n#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { printf(\"FAIL line %d: %s\\n\", __LINE__, #c); exit(1); } } while (0)\n\nint main(void) {\n  lut_init();\n  const double fs = 100e3; const int n = 100000;            /* 1 s of samples */\n  static uint16_t out[100000];\n  CHECK(dds_tuning(1000, fs) == 42949673u);\n  const double targets[] = {5.0, 50.0, 1000.0, 2500.5, 12345.0, 30000.0};\n  for (int k = 0; k < 6; k++) {\n    dds_t d = {0, dds_tuning(targets[k], fs)};\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) out[i] = dds_next(&d);\n    double exact = d.tuning * fs / 4294967296.0, meas = measure(out, n, fs);\n    double err = fabs(meas - targets[k]) / targets[k];\n    printf(\"target %9.3f Hz  M=%10u  exact %.6f Hz  measured %.4f Hz  (%.5f %%)\\n\", targets[k], d.tuning, exact, meas, 100 * err);\n    CHECK(err < 0.001);                                      /* within 0.1 % */\n    CHECK(fabs(exact - targets[k]) <= fs / 4294967296.0);    /* within one resolution step */\n  }\n  /* amplitude and shape: the output tracks an ideal sine to within the table's phase step */\n  dds_t d = {0, dds_tuning(1000, fs)}; double worst = 0;\n  for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {\n    uint32_t a = d.acc; double ideal = 2047.5 + 2047.5 * sin(2 * PI * (a / 4294967296.0));\n    double e = fabs(dds_next(&d) - ideal); if (e > worst) worst = e;\n  }\n  printf(\"worst deviation from the ideal sine: %.1f LSB (bound 2047.5*2*pi/256 = %.1f)\\n\", worst, 2047.5 * 2 * PI / 256);\n  CHECK(worst <= 2047.5 * 2 * PI / 256 + 0.5);\n  CHECK(lut[0] == 2048 && lut[64] == 4095 && lut[192] == 0);\n  printf(\"PASS\\n\");\n  return 0;\n}"}]}